Socket buffers on NetBSD
========================

libknet asks for 8 MB send and receive buffers on every socket.  With
NetBSD's default kern.sbmax (262144) the kernel refuses that size, and
libknet settles for the largest it is given, 128 KB.

That is enough for an unprivileged handle, which logs the cap and
carries on.  A privileged handle, which is what corosync opens when it
runs as root, treats the cap as an error (_configure_sockbuf() in
libknet/transport_common.c) and the link is not created.
Raise the limit before starting corosync, in /etc/sysctl.conf:

	kern.sbmax=16777216

With that value both UDP and local datagram sockets get the full 8 MB
(measured on NetBSD 11.0/amd64).
